194
00:14:37,291 --> 00:14:38,791
There are no fish.

195
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:41,333
They are just gone.

196
00:14:44,416 --> 00:14:47,166
I remember when my grandmother was chief.

197
00:14:47,250 --> 00:14:49,625
A hurricane kept the fish away for weeks.

198
00:14:50,208 --> 00:14:53,291
But they had dried fish stores
and fresh coconuts.

199
00:14:53,791 --> 00:14:57,166
They were prepared to wait
until the fish came back.

200
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:58,958
And they did come back.

201
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:01,083
But there is no hurricane.

202
00:15:01,625 --> 00:15:04,791
And even then, the lagoon was never empty.

203
00:15:04,875 --> 00:15:08,083
There's always a solution.
We just need to look for it.

204
00:15:08,166 --> 00:15:09,625
Ow!

205
00:15:17,916 --> 00:15:19,583
If the lagoon is empty,

206
00:15:20,583 --> 00:15:22,791
